@0    = ~Oh! Where did you come from? I-I was merely admiring the great stonework of these walls. I've not done anything else. I mean, what else would I be touching the stones for? I'll be leaving, then.~
@1    = ~Oh—there *is* a letter! I thought it was gone... Ahem. Good day to you, dear <PRO_SIRMAAM>.~
@2    = ~Oh, he didn't reply... My letter is gone, so he must have taken it... It was such a good hiding place. But no reply...~
@3    = ~I must apologize. I took your letter without realizing the consequences.~
@4    = ~I must apologize. I took your correspondence without realizing the consequences.~
@5    = ~It was a crappy hiding place. I found your correspondence.~
@6    = ~Whoops, I knew I shouldn't have taken it.~
@7    = ~Maybe, you know, the letter was removed by other means. Someone found it, a mouse took it for its nest—that kind of thing.~
@8    = ~So, the letter is gone. So what? Go and fight for your love, girl! Do not let yourself be cast aside without hearing it from him, personally.~
@9    = ~Oh, yes. I am sure he has forgotten about you completely! This has to be the only reason for a missing reply, the signs are obvious!~
@10   = ~No, I took your precious letter. What would it be worth to you, hmm?~
@11   = ~I couldn't care less. I'll take my leave.~
@12   = ~You...?~
@13   = ~Yes. Here, take it back, and my apologies.~
@14   = ~Yes, I did, but I can't give them back. I do apologize.~
@15   = ~And I appreciated it very much. You know, as an adventurer you never know when you'll need to go behind some bushes.~
@16   = ~Yep, and they are gone. Best you get lost, too.~
@17   = ~Well, let's say I had your precious letter. What would it be worth to you, hmm?~
@18   = ~You—you think...?~
@19   = ~Actually, it was me who took your correspondence. Apologies. Here, take it back.~
@20   = ~Actually, it was me who took your correspondence, but I can't give it back. I do apologize.~
@21   = ~I do believe that you should not read too much into a missing letter, but should look for certainty.~
@22   = ~If there is no letter despite this being your hidden place for messages, then he is likely not *that* interested in you.~
@23   = ~No, I took your precious letter, and it is gone. Best you get lost, too.~
@24   = ~This conversation has gone on long enough. I'll take my leave.~
@25   = ~That—that's *disgusting*! Get away from me, you brute!~
@26   = ~I... I need to go to him, at *once*!~
@27   = ~Oh no! I feared this would happen!~
@28   = ~Well, thank you—I guess. Ugh, the secret hiding place was not so secret after all!~
@29   = ~You—you're such a brute!~
@30   = ~You—you're such a brute! Fine, take *this* in exchange.~
@31   = ~Ugh. Rude!~
